{"author":{"id":"585844baa6074d44d241f46aa7c9f21ff46653adf617d7f070fbfe327626c989"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794735262,"nonce":"jpwsO1OibdsiaiMom5GCOSDHIG8=","title":"hxn-gpu-webgpu: WebGPU in the browser through hxn's wasm build","message":"A driver library for a Haxe program compiled to wasm and run in a page: calls go to the browser's `navigator.gpu` through JavaScript glue, and shaders are hxnsl's `WGSL`, which the browser compiles itself. `LAYOUT` gives explicit bind group layouts, and `CONST_\u003cname\u003e` the pipeline constants.\n\nhlwgpu's web build (xgpu.wasm with gpu.mjs and its worker) is prior art for the glue and for a page losing the device.\n\nWhen the browser has no WebGPU, the program falls back to the WebGL2 driver.","files":null}]}